# Settings every deploy of the shop's server code shares (Firebase loads this file, then .env.<project>, which the
# deploy writes with each shop's or the shared system's own settings). Nothing secret goes here: it is committed.
#
# Google's functions runtime answers /robots.txt and /favicon.ico with an empty 404 before any function sees them,
# unless IGNORED_ROUTES says otherwise. The front door (frontDoor.js) answers each shop's robots.txt, so only the icon
# stays filtered. Without this line every shop's robots.txt is "not found" and search engines lose its sitemap line.
IGNORED_ROUTES="/favicon.ico"
